      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 70-year-old man developed anterior precordial ST elevation during coronary angiography in the presence of a normal left coronary artery. Injection of a proximally totally occluded right coronary artery caused occlusion of the conus branch. The electrocardiographic findings are shown, and the pathogenesis is discussed."},
